        <definition>int board_id</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>board_id</name>
        <qualifiedname>ndigo_init_parameters::board_id</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>8-bit board ID number. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This number is filled into each packet created by the board and is useful if data streams of multiple boards will be merged. If boards of different types that use a compatible data format are used in a system each board should get a unique ID.</para>
<para>Can be changed with <ref refid="ndigo__common__interface_8h_1a96f8d98125ac8e8f4c0f8103666b5192" kindref="member">ndigo_set_board_id()</ref>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
